1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,378
This video shows the INR trend sitting beside the consultation.

2
00:00:05,078 --> 00:00:08,572
And when a clinician edits an INR, they never lose what they have typed.

3
00:00:10,172 --> 00:00:19,485
This patient takes warfarin and has four INR results. The patient summary has an INR review card, with a chart and the target range as a shaded band.

4
00:00:20,612 --> 00:00:28,985
On the card are two buttons, one to edit the last INR, and one to record a new INR. On the right is the new INR trend button.

5
00:00:30,985 --> 00:00:35,898
Now I start a consultation. Under Consultation visits, Start consultation.

6
00:00:37,025 --> 00:00:39,393
I type a sentence into Interval History.

7
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:50,489
Then I make the workspace bigger, and click the INR trend button. The trend opens beside the consultation, my sentence is still there, and nothing asked me to discard it.

8
00:00:52,489 --> 00:00:59,723
With a sentence typed, I click Edit INR in the trend. The editor opens in its own window, and the consultation stays open.

9
00:01:00,649 --> 00:01:04,178
I change the INR value to 2.9, and press Save.

10
00:01:06,409 --> 00:01:09,694
The chart shows the new value, and my sentence is still there.

11
00:01:10,849 --> 00:01:13,263
Then I cancel the consultation, and discard it.

12
00:01:15,289 --> 00:01:18,330
Back on the summary, the card shows the new value too.

13
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:28,656
With a sentence typed, I click Record INR on the card. The standard INR Monitoring form opens in its own window, with no discard prompt.

14
00:01:29,610 --> 00:01:33,418
I choose the indication and the target range, and fill in the date tested.

15
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:39,754
I enter an INR value of 3.1, and answer No to the dose change.

16
00:01:41,010 --> 00:01:46,910
I press Save. The consultation is still there with my sentence, and the card and the chart show the new point.

17
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:58,037
This second patient has only one INR, and a chart needs two points. So the card shows one line: the value, the date, and the target range.

18
00:02:00,037 --> 00:02:06,900
A community clinician sees the same card and chart, but read only. There is no Edit button, and no Record button.

19
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:13,846
The INR trend is in the patient chart, and in a window docked beside the consultation.

20
00:02:14,546 --> 00:02:18,261
Edit INR opens in its own window, and keeps the whole entry.

21
00:02:18,961 --> 00:02:23,164
Record new INR uses the standard form, also in its own window.

22
00:02:23,864 --> 00:02:26,674
The consultation form itself has nothing new in it.

23
00:02:27,374 --> 00:02:36,197
One pull request, 228, replaces the earlier 224, 227 and distro 300.
